","HR/Ncbsc/Sp3ms","to way his"]],"x":[[4031008,4031008,4]],"xn":1}},"people":[{"id":"balaam_593","name":"Balaam","also":"","summary":"Lord of the people; foreigner or glutton, as interpreted by others, the son of Beor, was a man of some rank among the Midianites (Num. 31:8; comp. 16).","verses":59,"father":"Beor","mother":"","v":[1,2,3,10,12,15,25]},{"id":"beor_466","name":"Beor","also":"Bosor","summary":"The father of Balaam (Num. 22:5; 24:3, 15; 31:8).","verses":9,"father":"","mother":"","v":[3,15]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[5,17,19]},{"id":"agag_108","name":"Agag","also":"","summary":"A king of the Amalekites referred to by Balaam (Num. 24:7).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"balak_387","name":"Balak","also":"Balac","summary":"Empty; spoiler, a son of Zippor, and king of the Moabites (Num. 22:2, 4).","verses":41,"father":"Zippor","mother":"","v":[10,12,13,25]},{"id":"jesus_905","name":"Jesus","also":"Immanuel, Emmanuel, Messiah, Shiloh, Christ, Jesus Christ, Messias","summary":"Anointed, the Greek translation of the Hebrew word rendered “Messiah”, the official title of our Lord, occurring five hundred and fourteen times in the New Testament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[17]},{"id":"moab_2103","name":"Moab","also":"Moabitess, Moabitish, Moabites","summary":"Used to denote the people of Moab (Num. 22:3-14; Judg. 3:30; 2 Sam. 8:2; Jer. 48:11, 13).","verses":149,"father":"Lot","mother":"Daughter of Lot - Older","v":[17]},{"id":"seth_2504","name":"Seth","also":"Sheth","summary":"Appointed; a substitute, the third son of Adam and Eve (Gen. 4:25; 5:3).","verses":10,"father":"Adam","mother":"Eve","v":[17]},{"id":"esau_1216","name":"Esau","also":"Edom, Edomite","summary":"Hairy, Rebekah’s first-born twin son (Gen. 25:25). The name of Edom, “red”, was also given to him from his conduct in connection with the red lentil “pottage” for which he sold his birthright (30, 31).","verses":151,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[18]},{"id":"amalek_197","name":"Amalek","also":"","summary":"Dweller in a valley, the son of Eliphaz and grandson of Esau (Gen. 36:12; 1 Chr. 1:36); the chief of an Idumean tribe (Gen. 36:16).","verses":22,"father":"Eliphaz","mother":"Timna","v":[20]},{"id":"asshur_349","name":"Asshur","also":"","summary":"Second son of Shem (Gen. 10:22; 1 Chr. 1:17). He went from the land of Shinar and built Nineveh, etc. (Gen. 10:11, 12). He probably gave his name to Assyria, which is the usual translation of the word, although the form Asshur is sometimes retained (Num. 24:22, 24; Ezek. 27:23, etc.).","verses":5,"father":"Shem","mother":"","v":[22,24]},{"id":"eber_1030","name":"Eber","also":"Heber","summary":"The third post-duluvian patriach after Shem (Gen. 10:24; 11:14). He is regarded as the founder of the Hebrew race (10:21; Num. 24:24).","verses":12,"father":"Salah","mother":"","v":[24]}],"places":[{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[8]},{"id":"moab_815","name":"Moab","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.49916,"lon":35.78051,"summary":"The land of Moab (Jer. 48:24), called also the “country of Moab” (Ruth 1:2, 6; 2:6), on the east of Jordan and the Dead Sea, and south of the Arnon (Num. 21:13, 26).","verses":148,"v":[17]},{"id":"edom_357","name":"Edom","kind":"Region","lat":31.25,"lon":34.75,"summary":"Idumea (Isa. 34:5, 6; Ezek. 35:15). “The field of Edom” (Gen. 32:3), “the land of Edom” (Gen. 36:16), was mountainous (Obad. 1:8, 9, 19, 21).","verses":79,"v":[18]},{"id":"seir_1042","name":"Seir","kind":"Region","lat":30.73469,"lon":35.60625,"summary":"The name of a mountainous region occupied by the Edomites, extending along the eastern side of the Arabah from the south-eastern extremity of the Dead Sea to near the Akabah, or the eastern branch of the Red Sea.","verses":24,"v":[18]},{"id":"amalek_53","name":"Amalek","kind":"Region","lat":30.65977,"lon":34.83555,"summary":"A tribe that dwelt in Arabia Petraea, between the Dead Sea and the Red Sea. They were not the descendants of Amalek, the son of Eliphaz, for they existed in the days of Abraham (Gen. 14:7).","verses":18,"v":[20]},{"id":"asshur_109","name":"Asshur","kind":"City","lat":36.35941,"lon":43.15289,"summary":"Second son of Shem (Gen. 10:22; 1 Chr. 1:17). He went from the land of Shinar and built Nineveh, etc. (Gen. 10:11, 12). He probably gave his name to Assyria, which is the usual translation of the word, although the form Asshur is sometimes retained (Num. 24:22, 24; Ezek. 27:23, etc.).","verses":4,"v":[22,24]},{"id":"kain_664","name":"Kain","kind":"City","lat":31.5,"lon":35.16667,"summary":"A town of the Kenites, a branch of the Midianites (Josh. 15:57), on the east edge of the mountain above Engedi; probably the “nest in a rock” mentioned by Balaam (Num. 24:21).","verses":2,"v":[22]},{"id":"kittim_707","name":"Kittim","kind":"","lat":35.01831,"lon":33.20769,"summary":"(Gen. 10:4).","verses":2,"v":[24]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1109,1109,1109,7200,3588,2895,2895,3068,3068,1288,1288,3478,3808,3808,3808,1980,5173,6471,6471,6471,6471,7896,7896,7896,6440,6440,413,4057,4057],[1109,1109,5375,5375,7200,7200,3478,7931,7626,7626,7626,7307,7307,430,430,1961,5921,5921],[5375,5375,5375,5375,4912,4912,559,5002,5002,5002,5002,1109,1109,1121,1160,1160,5002,5002,1397,1397,1397,5869,5869,8365,8365],[5002,5002,8085,8085,8085,8085,561,561,410,410,834,2372,4236,4236,7706,7706,7706,5307,5307,5307,58